# Modal Components

All custom modals live in `src/components/modals/` and follow a consistent pattern.

## Bottom Sheet Modal (MarkAttendanceModal, BulkApproveModal)

```tsx
<Modal visible={visible} animationType="slide" transparent statusBarTranslucent onRequestClose={onDismiss}>
  <SafeAreaView style={styles.safe} edges={['top', 'left', 'right', 'bottom']}>
    <Pressable style={styles.backdrop} onPress={onDismiss} />
    <View style={styles.sheetWrap} pointerEvents="box-none">
      <View style={styles.sheet}>
        {/* handle bar → header → ScrollView body → fixed footer */}
      </View>
    </View>
  </SafeAreaView>
</Modal>
```

- `safe` has `backgroundColor: colors.overlay`
- `sheet` has `borderTopLeftRadius: 24, borderTopRightRadius: 24`
- Body uses `ScrollView` with `nestedScrollEnabled`, `bounces={false}`
- Footer has submit (primary bg) + cancel (text button)

## Centered Dialog (DatePicker, TimePicker)

```tsx
<Modal visible={visible} animationType="fade" transparent statusBarTranslucent>
  <SafeAreaView style={styles.safe}>
    <Pressable style={styles.backdrop} onPress={onDismiss} />
    <View style={styles.sheetWrap} pointerEvents="box-none">
      <View style={styles.sheet}>{/* centered card content */}</View>
    </View>
  </SafeAreaView>
</Modal>
```

## Imperative Hook Pattern

Modals use a `useXxx()` hook returning `{ props, present, dismiss }`:

```tsx
const { props: statusAlertProps, presentError, presentSuccess } = useStatusAlert();
const { props: confirmAlertProps, present: presentConfirm } = useConfirmAlert();
// Render: <StatusAlert {...statusAlertProps} />
```

## Chip Selectors

Reusable chip pattern for multi-option selection inside modals:

```tsx
<Pressable style={[styles.chip, active && styles.chipActive]}>
  <Text style={[styles.chipText, active && styles.chipTextActive]}>{label}</Text>
</Pressable>
```

Active chip: `borderColor: colors.primary`, light primary bg.
